{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>My soul refuses to touch</b> — the bruises that my soul refuses to touch, before they became the illnesses of my body." "Some say: לנגוע — like 'to weaken,' and similar to it: וינגוע את יהושע (Joshua 9:4). And the meaning: for my soul refuses, that it weaken and I die." "<b>They</b> — refers back to the straw."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:02:06.732434251Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}